-- title:
--   Parameter derivative of the Euler–Maclaurin integrand
-- statement:
--   Let $x>0$ and $s\in\mathbb C$, and put $F(s)=b_1(x)(-s)x^{-s-1}$, with
--   $b_1$ the first periodic Bernoulli sawtooth. Then $F$ has complex derivative
--   $$F'(s)=b_1(x)(-1+s\log x)x^{-s-1}.$$
--   The logarithm and power are the complex logarithm and complex power of $x$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/DrMurphyIsIn/Arda/blob/af4fde8972eb6d4e78c7d9a95933b18b81adf52d/telperion/examples/zeta_reflection/lean/EMZetaComplex.lean#L467-L494

